    {
        "content": "<p>I feel like the explanation in the manual is completely wrong? The universes of parameters are completely irrelevant, same with indices; but the level of every field type must be <code>≤</code> (not necessarily <code>&lt;</code>) the inductive types level; or more concretely: If we have an inductive type <code>inductive MyInduct (...) : ... → Sort u</code> and we have a constructor <code>| myCtor ... (x : α) ... : MyInduct ...</code> with <code>α : Sort v</code> then <code>v ≤ u ∨ u = 0</code> is required.</p>",
        "id": 606981614,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1782642990
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks. At the very least, the language reference is confusing. All examples that I have come up with are compatible with your formulation.</p>",
        "id": 606992561,
        "sender_full_name": "Lauri Oksanen",
        "timestamp": 1782654982
    }
